{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/348286-what-if-the-apocalypse-was-just-the-beginning","id":348286,"title":"What if the Apocalypse was just the beginning...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-23T07:22:02-08:00","id":348286,"title":"What if the Apocalypse was just the beginning...","content":"\u206cI have been musing over what a post apocalyptic World of Darkness might be like from the Grand Epicist's perspective. For instance, the Apocalypse happens, Gehenna is carried out, etc. Now, if the Fae are agents of the Wyld and Mages are agents of the Weaver - then it strikes true with me for Vampires to be the disenfranchised agents of the Bringer of Harmony.<br /> <br /> What if the real Apocalypse, the real Gehenna, isn't the destruction of Existence, but the Freeing of the Wyrm from the bonds of the Weaver? Further, the only means to accomplish this is the slaying of the Wyrm - resulting in something wraithlike which has the experience of everything the Bringer of Harmony was, and is the Bringer of Harmony by nature - but with the Wyrm for a Shadow.<br /> <br /> Further, the process of killing the Wyrm killed everything else also - but the tapestry wasn't lost, and that brief moment of non-existence was refueled by the power of the Wyld. Now the universe is held together by a Wyld weakened through its efforts, a Weaver devastated by its failure, a Bringer of Harmony full of angst and on the mend from the trauma of extreme captivity, and the entire lot of them so worn down the world seems much more mundane. Everything that existed when the Apocalypse began re-exists. The Bringer of Harmony is attempting to do just that - but is struggling with the shadows of its Trauma, its anger at Weaver and Wyld, etc.<br /> <br /> The universe seems calm, the balance seems restored, the moment is a picnic on a gentle summer's day. Even the remnants of the Garou are celebrating the Victory. And the Storm is just out of sight on the horizon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T09:26:56-08:00","id":348378,"title":"","content":"Nice story. But to what end do you want to use This?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T03:28:45-08:00","id":349731,"title":"","content":"The purpose is the exploration of ideas. CWoD began an apocalypse, one with which I was unsatisfied. And I remember a discussion between a OC Tzimisce and some others with a Nefandi. The Nefandi indicated they preferred the Creation-Destruction-Creation theory of the universe. That is the end is not the End but the beginning. Sort of like a Yuga in the spiral dance of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T05:19:49-08:00","id":349789,"title":"","content":"Not all mages are agents of the weaver. Dynamac Avatars could be said to follow wild with Jhor Resonance and its Avatars following Destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T09:19:21-08:00","id":349881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/348286-what-if-the-apocalypse-was-just-the-beginning?p=349731#post349731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purpose is the exploration of ideas. CWoD began an apocalypse, one with which I was unsatisfied. And I remember a discussion between a OC Tzimisce and some others with a Nefandi. The Nefandi indicated they preferred the Creation-Destruction-Creation theory of the universe. That is the end is not the End but the beginning. Sort of like a Yuga in the spiral dance of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a Nephandi recruiter's patter... I would take it with a Dead Sea and a Bonneville Flats worth of salt.<br /> <br /> Decension would probably be more like Creation-Destruction- Eternal Void (perhaps ruled over by some infernal power/the Conquerer Wyrmh/other tentacled monstrosities). Break the wheel of time. End the dance. Those are all aberrations in the continuity of blessed, unending unBeing. &quot;Peace&quot; without End.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:02:18-08:00","id":350366,"title":"","content":"Interesting things to note:<br /> <br /> - W:TA actually does tend to conjecture that an Apocalypse wouldn't end everything, most likely. What everyone is fighting for is the shape that the next world will take.<br /> - Freeing the Wyrm from the binding of the Pattern Web that the Weaver inflicted on it is a canonical possibility. In the Weaver Ascendant scenario of Apocalypse, the most favorable end results in this happening. It also practically destroys everything in the cosmos, leaving room for renewal. The resulting new cosmos would probably not have vampires in it, among other things, on account of it not being bricked by incomprehensibly huge spirits going awry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T05:23:38-08:00","id":350573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/348286-what-if-the-apocalypse-was-just-the-beginning?p=349881#post349881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descension would probably be more like Creation-Destruction- Eternal Void (perhaps ruled over by some infernal power/the Conqueror Wyrm/other tentacled monstrosities). Break the wheel of time. End the dance. Those are all aberrations in the continuity of blessed, unending unBeing. &quot;Peace&quot; without End.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, there is more than one way to skin a Nefandus. I worked from the perspective of my own paradigm, that the three are intricately connected in a single pattern of Existence. Just as each highlight, middle-tone, and shadow has its own highlight, middle-tone, and shadow, so also the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm are sources of the refraction we artistically call highlight, middle-tone, and shadow. They are the unending wheel of themselves, dancing through time, in the endless creation, preservation, and confirmation of Existing. The skin you presented appears as the linear motion from creation through preservation to annihilation. This is a choice of theme: hope vs. hopelessness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/348286-what-if-the-apocalypse-was-just-the-beginning?p=350366#post350366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W:tA actually does tend to conjecture that an Apocalypse wouldn't end everything, most likely. What everyone is fighting for is the shape that the next world will take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kipling wrote &quot;Anger is the egg of Fear.&quot; From that I extract a pattern of behavior equal to Faith is the assurance of those things in which we Hope. What we hope for is the profitability of our paradigm, and when that is threatened we respond with greater Anger the greater the realization of that Fear. Faith is the shape of that next world - whether the faith of the Technomancer, the Traditionalist, the Sluagh, the Giovanni, and all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Freeing the Wyrm from the binding of the Pattern Web that the Weaver inflicted on it is a canonical possibility. In the Weaver Ascendant scenario of Apocalypse, the most favorable end results in this happening. </div> </div> </div>Favorable is a status quo approach. All we really may surmise from the lore is that something the Bringer of Harmony was going to remove was sufficient to cause the Weaver perform a crime of passion. We do not know what would have resulted from recycling through the Wyld - assuming the quantum flow is cyclic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also practically destroys everything in the cosmos, leaving room for renewal. The resulting new cosmos would probably not have vampires in it, among other things, on account of it not being bricked by incomprehensibly huge spirits going awry. </div> </div> </div>Agreed that is a possibility. I certainly can see how the pent up &quot;dark-matter&quot; explosion. But could the Weaver and Wyld manage to pull a renewel through the event? In otherwords, nothing unreal exists, and as long as there is existence that which is real continues. I am not convinced vampires, or any other supernatural can cease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T09:49:20-08:00","id":350710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/348286-what-if-the-apocalypse-was-just-the-beginning?p=350573#post350573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Certainly, there is more than one way to skin a Nefandus. I worked from the perspective of my own paradigm, that the three are intricately connected in a single pattern of Existence. Just as each highlight, middle-tone, and shadow has its own highlight, middle-tone, and shadow, so also the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm are sources of the refraction we artistically call highlight, middle-tone, and shadow. They are the unending wheel of themselves, dancing through time, in the endless creation, preservation, and confirmation of Existing. The skin you presented appears as the linear motion from creation through preservation to annihilation. This is a choice of theme: hope vs. hopelessness.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming a fundamental underlying truth - the Cycle CANNOT be broken. That's an assumption that a lot, probably most, and perhaps all by a few (who may be self-deluded) Nephandi will buy into. In many ways that's exactly what the Nephandi are all about, the Wyrm is all about, the Yama Kings are all about. The universe is supposed to work in a certain elegant way. And they want to smash it, tear it, derail it, break it. <br /> <br /> Now maybe that's ALWAYS the way it's been or maybe that's the way it HAS to be... For the Cycle to turn there have to be people who want it to not turn. And they are part of way that it works. Their necessary belief in their ability to affect the unaffectable is an inherent part of the system, but it's doomed to futility. The only true hopelessness is that of those who want to doom others to hopelessness, because they are doomed to failure.<br /> <br /> But, if that's an underlying assumption, it's got to be laid out there: There is no Apocalypse because all things that move toward Apocalypse, move through and past it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:03:18-08:00","id":350820,"title":"","content":"Indeed and its worth noting that virtually all the ToJ scenarios from <i>Ends of Empire</i> to <i>Time of Judgement</i> have the world surviving beyond whatever Armageddon comes for it. Even <i>Ascension's</i> Nephandi Victory scenario ends with a bit of fiction set a hundred years after the Nephandi and their Gods have taken over the world and has an older Mage showing a group of people with Avatars on the verge of Awakening that things aren't lost, that the world can emerge the hell its in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T13:38:30-08:00","id":351938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/348286-what-if-the-apocalypse-was-just-the-beginning?p=350710#post350710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now maybe that's ALWAYS the way it's been or maybe that's the way it HAS to be... For the Cycle to turn there have to be people who want it to not turn. And they are part of way that it works. Their necessary belief in their ability to affect the unaffectable is an inherent part of the system, but it's doomed to futility. The only true hopelessness is that of those who want to doom others to hopelessness, because they are doomed to failure.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You realize this just defined Siddhartha Gautama as one of the Nephandi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T08:34:30-08:00","id":352723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/348286-what-if-the-apocalypse-was-just-the-beginning?p=351938#post351938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You realize this just defined Siddhartha Gautama as one of the Nephandi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but probably not. A Nephandi might use Buddhism as good patter, but Nephandi stop at the Void. That's their goal. Void might or might not equal Nirvana. Probably not, considering the way that the Nephandi and their goals have been depicted to date and the way most Buddhist sects from the beginning until now define it. <br /> <br /> Like the cycle of existence itself, I go back to the beginning of what I said. If a Nephandi is trying to sell you on joining him in Decension, check your pockets for your wallet and your Pattern for your soul. You're being had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}